# What builds cellular-settings (packages/cellular-settings): the Rust
# toolchain and the GTK 4 and libadwaita development files of the Ubuntu
# suite. ci/Dockerfile.cellular-settings installs this list into its image;
# without docker, scripts/build-cellular-settings.sh has the arm64 buildd
# chroot install it (lib-buildd.sh). "#" starts a comment.
#
# rustc: the gtk4 crate (0.11) needs 1.92 or later; resolute has 1.93. The
# binary is linked against the release's own libraries, so it is built in the
# release: its GTK 4 here, and its glibc.
build-essential pkg-config cargo rustc
# cargo fetches the crates over TLS, and the base image has no certificates
ca-certificates
# the toolkit
libgtk-4-dev libadwaita-1-dev
# the Chinese catalog: msgfmt, at build time
gettext
# the package, and the check that the binary is an arm64 executable
dpkg-dev debhelper fakeroot file
# in the image only: ci/cellular-settings.sh runs make in tmux inside the container
tmux
# in the image only: broadway, the headless display of GTK, on which the program
# on the phone renders a page at any size (packages/cellular-settings/README.md)
libgtk-4-bin
